# Mongoid-like document's and a plain class's own `scope` answered
# `Relation#where` at 1.0. Only a model's scope — a class under
# ActiveRecord::Base, or a module one includes — runs on the relation; the
# rest run where they are written. And the relation Rails builds delegates a
# model class method Kernel also answers (`display`) ahead of Kernel's.
